# Machine-local JDK-home mapping for dependency-auto-update-tool.
#
# This file is DELIBERATELY NOT committed to git (see ../.gitignore) -- a JDK
# installation path is a fact about one machine, not a repo-wide policy every
# clone should share (tech-stack-decisions.md, NFR Requirements Q1a).
#
# Copy this template to "jdk-home.local.properties" (same directory) and set
# real paths for your machine before running the tool for the first time:
#
#   cp jdk-home.local.properties.template jdk-home.local.properties
#
# One entry per branch declared in ../config/tool.properties's
# branch.<name>.expectedJdkMajor policy (business-rules.md BR-3) -- this
# tool's own reference deployment, tamacat-httpd, declares two branches with
# different JDK baselines, verified against the live repository:
#   master      -> JDK 8
#   v2.0-tc11   -> JDK 25
#
# The tool validates that whatever path you set here actually reports that
# branch's expected major version (via <path>/bin/java -version) before it
# will run any detection/validation for that branch -- it never falls back
# to its own running JVM, which targets a modern Java version independent of
# either branch.

jdkHome.master=/path/to/your/jdk-8
jdkHome.v2.0-tc11=/path/to/your/jdk-25
